feedback.body:
Using the flexible array member syntax instead of `char info[0]` is totally fine, I had just forgot about its existence :)
I forgot to add a field for data size, so it'd be
```
struct packet {
    struct packet *prev;
    struct packet *next;
    struct address addresses[N];
    datetime_t ts;
    size_t payloadSize;
    uint8_t payload[];
}
```
In addition to the single malloc, you can access the payload with `packet->payload[i]`

