feedback.body:
@ranguli when applying the changes, please use [fixup commits](https://moodledev.io/general/development/abc/fixups) instead of adding the changes on top with the "Fix ..." commits. This allows to do a git rebase with autosquash and keep the history clean.

Another thing: with the current implementation, the current position of the TX power selection array is reset to zero each time the radio is power-cycled. This means that, instead of having the progression 1W > 2.5W > 5W, the selection will always "jump" to 1W and move one step forward each time the key 6 is pressed.
Probably this sequence can be handled better using a `switch` statement based on the value of `state.channel.power`. See my comment here: https://github.com/OpenRTX/OpenRTX/pull/358/changes#r2366272402

Given that the UI allows to cycle through the power levels only along one direction, I think that we can adopt a KISS approach and use a `switch` statement, eventually wrapped in a dedicated function.

Something like this:
```
static uint32_t _ui_getNextPowerLevel(uint32_t curr)
{
    switch(curr) {
        case 1000:
            return 2500;
            break;

        case 2500:
            return 5000;
            break;

        default:
            return 1000;
    }
}
```
This has the extra advantage that, in case the power level assumes some borked values, it will always be assigned a sane default.

