feedback.body:
Three observations:
1) I saw that, when bringing in the specification for the linux code style, some configs are gone: I have to go through them and see which ones should be kept;
2) I prefer not to have the commit passing the entire repository through the clang-format: even though it makes sense doing so, I think is a change too much intrusive. It will also generate an enormous pile of merge conficts with the branches currently under development and the PRs;
3) I'm afraid that automating the linting via github actions is again too much intrusive. The point is that clang-format is blindly applying the specified set of rules and, in doing so, it can make the the code look worse than it was before the linting pass.

